      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016. Published by Elsevier Masson SAS.",
        "AbstractText": "A 41-year-old patient, with a medical history of embryonal carcinoma treated by orchidectomy at the age of 27, presented with abdominal pain. Serum alphafetoprotein, β-HCG and CEA levels were normal. MRI showed a cystic retroperitoneal lesion with septation, measuring 20cm. He underwent a surgical resection. Histology revealed an adenocarcinoma arising on a mature multitissular teratoma."
      },
